{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And it was, when the Ark set out.</b> It is taught: Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel says — this passage is destined to be uprooted from here and written in its place. And why was it written here? To interrupt between 'the people were as complainers' and 'they set out from Mount HaShem' — for both are calamities. And where is its place? Rabbi Yosi said: among the standards, i.e., immediately after 'and the Kohathites, bearers of the sanctuary, set out' etc. — 'And it was, when the Ark set out' etc." "<b>And Moses said: Arise, YHWH.</b> Because the cloud would depart from above the Mishkan at the time of the journeys."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:18.949094190Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}